# nr-office-author-pptx-build: the HTML deck builder and runner of crate mixdog-office-author. What the lead applies (all of it is
# in files this task does not own). It was not compiled by this task (no cargo run).

## 0. The chart wiring of nr-office-author-pptx-charts must be applied first
pptx_build.rs calls `Presentation::add_chart(index, kind, data, options)` and names `AxisStyle`, `ChartData`, `ChartKind`,
`ChartLayout`, `ChartOptions` and `GridLine` from `crate::pptx_writer`. Those are items 2, 3 and 4 of
`nr-office-author-pptx-charts.wire` (the `mod charts;` / `mod chart_workbook;` lines and the `pub use charts::{...}` line in
pptx_writer/mod.rs, the `Slide` chart object and `Presentation::add_chart` in slide.rs and presentation.rs). In the tree
this task was written against they are not applied yet (pptx_writer/mod.rs has no `mod charts;`), so the crate cannot compile
before them.

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-author/src/lib.rs
Beside `pub mod pptx_writer;` add:

    pub mod pptx_build;
    pub mod pptx_html_runner;

and extend the crate doc by one sentence: `pptx_build` is the HTML deck builder (`authoring/pptx-html-build.mjs`: the measure the
browser read becomes native text boxes, shapes, lines, tables, charts and pictures on the pptx writer) and `pptx_html_runner` the
HTML deck runner (`authoring/pptx-html-runner.mjs`: measure, build, normalise, keep `<deck>.mixdog-source.html` and the page
images, the drift of the render against the HTML, the comparison images).

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-author/Cargo.toml
Nothing to add: every crate the two modules and the twin test use (base64, serde_json, url, mixdog-core-api, mixdog-fsio,
mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base, mixdog-ooxml, mixdog-raster, mixdog-rt; dev: async-trait, tokio, mixdog-testkit, mixdog-rt with
test-support) is in the manifest already. `serde_json` must keep `preserve_order` (the result JSON lists its keys in the order
Node does; measure_deck's tests already rely on it). Cargo.lock and mixdog-workspace-hack: no change.

